  "summary_en": "Tennessee bill (HB 2365/SB 2836) defining personal delivery devices (sidewalk delivery robots) and exempting them from motor vehicle law. It sets operating rules: yield to pedestrians, 10 mph limit in pedestrian areas, lighting, braking, owner ID marker, $100,000 liability insurance, and local authority to ban them. Effective July 1, 2020.",
